C2 -- precision on kappa to separate 1/2 from its nearest DISTINCT surviving rival at 3 sigma
====================================================================================================
  nearest distinct rival to 1/2: Verlinde 2016, a0 = cH0/6 at kappa = 0.4824, Delta = 0.0176
  3-sigma separation needs sigma(kappa) <= 0.0059 = 1.17% of kappa
  [PASS] C2 the nearest DISTINCT rival to 1/2 is closer than today's kappa error, so the data do not separate them at 3 sigma
         measured: Delta = 0.0176, needs 1.17% (sigma<= 0.0059); best band sigma ~ 0.043 gives 0.41 sigma
         reading:  reproduces k03: ~2.8% on a_0 needed for 3 sigma vs a 9.47% mass-budget floor; here 1.2% needed
  [PASS] C2b the CKN/seesaw a0 = Lambda_DE^2/(2 M_Pl) is EXACTLY kappa = 1/2 (a restatement of the density identity), so it can never be separated from the framework -- it carries no independent content
         measured: kappa_seesaw = 0.5000 (= 1/2 by construction)
         reading:  consistent with L260: a0 = Lambda_DE^2/(2 M_Pl) is the density identity in seesaw notation

